{"id": "0000133c-0000-4000-8000-00000000133c", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit the Lambda functions in us-east-1 in two parallel passes. One covers function configuration (runtime, memory, timeout, tracing, VPC, DLQ, permissions and so on). The other covers runtime behavior from CloudWatch metrics (errors, throttles, duration against timeout, concurrency). Each pass will record what it could and couldn't check, so I can give you a grounded confidence level.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_Ed2dRPjiqPQLAUy16XpLMd", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "lambda-config-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit ALL Lambda functions in us-east-1 for CONFIGURATION against serverless best practices. Read-only.",
  "context": "User wants a best-practices audit of Lambda functions in us-east-1 plus an honest confidence assessment. Agent space account is 123456789012. Use list_associations to see whether other associated AWS accounts exist; if so, cover each (state which accounts you covered and which you could not access). This slice covers configuration only; a parallel sub-agent covers CloudWatch runtime metrics, so do not duplicate that.",
  "resources": ["lambda us-east-1", "account 123456789012"],
  "criteria": "Enumerate every function with full pagination (record the total count). For each, use list_functions / get_function_configuration / get_function_concurrency / get_function_event_invoke_config / list_event_source_mappings / get_policy / list_function_url_configs / list_tags as relevant. Check: deprecated or soon-to-be-deprecated runtimes (verify current deprecation dates via verify_aws_claim, don't rely on memory); memory and timeout settings (default 128MB / 3s or max 900s timeout); X-Ray/active tracing; DLQ or on-failure destinations for async invokes; retry config; reserved/provisioned concurrency; VPC config (without need, or single-AZ/subnet); env var secrets in plaintext or no KMS key; execution role breadth (e.g. AdministratorAccess or wildcard * actions - read role policies only); resource policy with public principal '*'; function URLs with AuthType NONE; architecture (arm64/Graviton opportunity); log group retention (never-expire) and logging config; package type/size and layers; SnapStart for Java where relevant; tags; event source mapping settings (batch size, partial batch response, DLQ). Output: a table or compact list of findings per category with function names and severity (High/Med/Low), a per-category count of functions affected, and a summary. IMPORTANT for confidence: explicitly report (a) total functions found vs. functions actually inspected, (b) any API calls that failed or were access-denied, (c) any checks you could not perform, (d) any assumptions or inferences vs directly observed facts. Keep the report concise; do not dump raw JSON."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Lambda function configurations in us-east-1"}, {"id": "tooluse_w8HsVW49LJn2CrIuWx9hro", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "lambda-metrics-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Assess runtime behavior of ALL Lambda functions in us-east-1 from CloudWatch metrics over the last 14 days (ending 2026-11-17T20:00:00Z) to flag best-practice issues. Read-only.",
